codex
Built a viable native Track B generator based on Section 4, Proposition 4.1 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.05218).

Local results:

- 0/200,000 structured guesses.
- Four attacks: 0/8 each.
- Hopcroft–Karp: 4,031 edge inspections.
- Compact affine route: 222 operations.
- Answer: 884 characters, 249 atoms.
- All local gates pass.

Files:

- [gen_2503_05218.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218/gen_2503_05218.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218/README.md)
- [failed oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [superseded prior rejection](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218/PRIOR_REJECTION.md)

The result is not yet shippable: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” four times, producing zero counted oracle attempts. No failures were misreported as hardness evidence, and the hinted/placebo transcripts were not fabricated.

Once the OpenRouter allowance is restored, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2503_05218.py
```

Then run the isolated structural and placebo G9 arms.
