The completed `easy` arm exposed a design weakness: all three models solved the long explicit factor, while the current “compact” route still spends 222 operations and 249 answer atoms. I’m tightening the same Proposition 4.1 family to use a fixed-size symbolic witness—two affine matching formulas—which keeps the paper’s triangle-factor object but lets difficulty grow in the graph rather than in transcription.
