codex
Implemented a native Track B generator based on Section 4, Proposition 4.1 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.05218).

Key results:

- Four-integer symbolic triangle-factor certificate.
- Structure-aware guess rate: `1/1,200,000`; exact probability `4.386e-7`.
- Reference search: up to 32,490 membership tests.
- Compact route: 94 exact operations.
- All local G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Answer size: 34 characters, 4 atoms.

Deliverables:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218/gen_2503_05218.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2503.05218/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The result is not yet shippable: every oracle request returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” Consequently, the transcripts contain four errors each and zero counted attempts; no model failure or hardness verdict has been fabricated. Once quota is restored, the bare hardening loop and both G9 arms must be rerun.
